finding: crates/physics/src/events.rs:20,27,35 use the eight-byte Id (u16 generation) for contact IDs, departing from Box3D include/box3d/id.h:68-74 (b3ContactId has padding and u32 generation) and types.h:1120,1142,1158. id() at events.rs:151 truncates contact generation, and kernel/eventbuffers.ts:27 decodes only that truncated halfword. At generation 65536, begin/end/hit delivery returns generation 0; valid contacts become invalid public handles and finish_contacts' generation guard cannot fill the promised begin impulse. ContactEnd should contain 28 bytes, and authorized ContactBegin should append its impulse after the 28-byte native record, not after 24 bytes. The purported native-layout proof at events.rs:411-413 asserts the incorrect layout. Independently reproduced in a git archive 621e7d20 scratch tree by setting a resident contact's generation to 65536 and publishing its begin event: expected 65536, received 0. Ordinary output golds never exercise this generation, so their Check passes despite the failure.
